      ],
      "text": "Faculty Profiles Back to Faculty Profiles Stephanie Lindsey Assistant Professor, MAE Fluid mechanics, numerical analysis, cradiovascular development biology Lindsey’s work lies at the interface of fluid mechanics, numerical analysis and cardiovascular developmental biology. She seeks to determine causal-effect relationships for the creation of cardiac malformations and address important challenges in clinical treatment of congenital heart defects through a combined computational-experimental approach. Capsule Bio: Before joining UC San Diego in 2021, Lindsey was a postdctoral researcher at Stanford Univeristy. She earned a Ph.D. from Cornell University. Update your profile Dr. Stephanie Lindsey Congenital Anomaly Research Laboratory (CARL)",
